From 5a1c0de000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:50:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: broadcom: us-48-500w: Add a ramoops region

1 MiB of DDR in the high bank for pstore (ramoops): the boot health
record (boot counter, clean-shutdown flag) is written to pmsg and read
back at the next boot, so no flash is written.

The region is above the 64 MiB a2 carveout and 4 MiB below the top of
DDR, clear of the bootloader image relocated to 0x6ff40000. Whether the
DDR keeps its contents over a soft or watchdog reset is not measured;
the health line reports rec=ram/prev=none when it does not.

Signed-off-by: TODO
---
 .../boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
@@ -44,6 +44,16 @@
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reg = <0x04000000 0x04000000>;
 			reusable;
+		};
+
+		/* us48-health boot record (pstore pmsg, RAM only): above the a2 carveout, below uboot-1's image at 0x6ff40000 */
+		ramoops@6fc00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x6fc00000 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+			record-size = <0x10000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x40000>;
 		};
 	};
 
